    "sentences": [{"text":"A) An abnormal winter snow storm. B) The first warm front from Europe. C) The frequent choking smog. D) The unusual warm winter.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) From Saturday afternoon. B) From this Friday. C) In the next spring. D) During the Christmas holiday.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) The project of free digital off-line resources in Nigeria. B) The project of free video lessons in Nigeria. C) The digital library in Ahmadu Bello University. D) The non-profit organizations in Ahmadu Bello University.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Multimedia work. C) Informative websites. B) Digital documents. D) Computer software.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It hit another car. C) It hit a driving bus in the road. B) It was overspeed. D) It hit a Lexus SUV.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) 3 kilometers per hour. C) 24 kilometers per hour. B) 6 kilometers per hour. D) 180 kilometers per hour.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Realities of speed and distance. C) Wheel and fender damage. B) Accidents in the road. D) Driving buses in the road.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) From some of her friends. C) From a telephone directory. B) From the wanted column. D) From a television commercial.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) She finished her secondary school. B) She studied in a vocational college. C) She graduated from an open university. D) She received full-time education abroad.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) She teaches an evening class. C) She is a policewoman. B) She works as a tour guide. D) She is a shorthand-typist.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) A job in a travel agency. C) A job as a policewoman. B) A job in the government. D) A job as a teacher.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It was interrupted for four years. B) It has been off and on for ten years. C) It helps enlarge his customer network. D) It provides him with career opportunities.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Traditional setting. C) Social games. B) Individualized service. D) Home-made beer.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) The quality of beer. C) The atmosphere. B) The owner's attitude.. D) The right location.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It makes retirees feel useful. C) It is a profitable business. B) It helps old people kill time. D) It is a rather tough job.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It helps the user to escape reality. B) It is becoming increasingly popular. C) It hurts a person and those around them. D) It gives rise to serious social instability.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) They take drugs to get high. B) They use drugs just for fun. C) They use drugs as medicine. D) They keep drug use a secret.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It is fatal to the user. B) It is hard to get rid of. C) It is the cause of various social problems. D) It is quite common in entertainment circles.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Taking up exercises after recovery. B) Finding new ways to cure heart disease. C) Going on a diet upon leaving the hospital. D) Producing tasty healthy frozen food.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It was carefully tested with consumers. B) It was disapproved by many diet experts. C) It was promoted by health organizations. D) It was highly expected by the general public.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Competitive price. C) Low expectations. B) Vigorous promotion. D) Unique ingredients.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It has a positive implication for consumers. B) It tricks the elders into impulse purchasing. C) It matches the food's dark green packaging. D) It was suggested by the firm's vice-president.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It will be abolished sooner or later. B) It is practiced in most of the states. C) It has to be approved by the Supreme Court. D) It has drawn a lot of criticism from overseas.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) What effect it might have on youngsters. B) What type of criminals should receive it. C) Whether there should be a minimum age limit for execution. D) Whether the practice should be allowed to continue in future.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) The court sentenced him to life in prison for killing two friends. B) The governor changed his death sentence to life in prison. C) He was the first minor to be executed in South Carolina. D) He was sentenced to death for a crime he committed as a minor.","start":0,"end":0}],
