    "sentences": [{"text":"A) Land a space vehicle on the moon in 2019.1.A)Land a space vehicle on the moon in 2019. B) Design a new generation of mobile phones.) Design a new generation of mobile phones. C) Set up a mobile phone network on the moon.) Set up a mobile phone network on the moon. D) Gather data from the moon with a tiny device.)Gather data from the moon with a tiny device.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It is stable..A)It is stable. B) It is durable.)It is durable. C) It is inexpensive. ) It is inexpensive. D) It is sophisticated.) It is sophisticated.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It lasted more than six hours..A)It lasted more than six hours. B) No injuries were yet reported.) No injuries were yet reported. C) Nobody was in the building when it broke out.) Nobody was in the building when it broke out. D) It had burned for 45 minutes by the time firefighters arrived.D)It had burned for 45 minutes by the time firefighters arrived.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Recruit and train more firefighters.4.A)Recruit and train more firefighters. B) Pull down the deserted shopping mall.) Pull down the deserted shopping mall. C) Turn the shopping mall into an amusement park.)Turn the shopping mall into an amusement park. D) Find money to renovate the local neighborhood.) Find money to renovate the local neighborhood.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Shrinking potato farming. .A) Shrinking potato farming. B) Heavy reliance on import.) Heavy reliance on import. C) Widespread plant disease. ) Widespread plant disease. D) Insufficient potato supply.) Insufficient potato supply.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It intends to keep its traditional diet.. A) It intends to keep its traditional diet. B) It wants to expand its own farming.B)It wants to expand its own farming. C) It is afraid of the spread of disease.) It is afraid of the spread of disease. D) It is worried about unfair competition.) It is worried about unfair competition.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Global warming. 7.A) Global warming. B) Ever-rising prices.) Ever-rising prices. C) Government regulation. ) Government regulation. D) Diminishing investment.) Diminishing investment.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Informative. .A) Informative. B) Inspiring.) Inspiring. C) Dull. )Dull. D) Shallow.) Shallow.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) She types on a keyboard. .A) She types on a keyboard. B) She does recording.) She does recording. C) She takes photos. ) She takes photos. D) She takes notes. She takes notes.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It keeps her mind active. 10.A)It keeps her mind active. B) It makes her stay awake.B) It makes her stay awake. C) It enables her to think hard.) It enables her to think hard. D) It helps her kill time.) It helps her kill time.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It enables her to improve her pronunciation.11.A) It enables her to improve her pronunciation. B) It helps her better remember what she learns.)It helps her better remember what she leams. C) It turns out to be an enjoyable way of learning.)It turns out to be an enjoyable way of learning. D) It proves to be far more effective than writing.D)It proves to be far more effective than writing.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) To spend her honeymoon.12. A) To spend her honeymoon. B) To try authentic Indian food.) To try authentic Indian food. C) To take photos of the Taj Mahal.) To take photos of the Taj Mahal. D) To trace the origin of a love story.D)To trace the origin of a love story.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) In memory of a princess.3.A) In memory of a princess. B) In honor of a great emperor.B) In honor of a great emperor. C) To mark the death of an emperor of the 1600s.)To mark the death of an emperor of the 1600s. D) To celebrate the birth of a princess’s 14th child.)To celebrate the birth of a princess's 14th child.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It looks older than expected.14.A)It looks older than expected. B) It is built of wood and bricks.) It is built of wood and bricks. C) It stores lots of priceless antiques.)It stores lots of priceless antiques. D) It has walls decorated with jewels.)It has walls decorated with jewels.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Their streets are narrow.5.A) Their streets are narrow. B) They are mostly crowded.) They are mostly crowded. C) Each one has a unique character.)Each one has a unique character. D) Life can be tedious in some places.) Life can be tedious in some places.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) They help spread the latest technology.16.A)They help spread the latest technology. B) They greatly enrich people’s leisure life.) They greatly enrich people's leisure life. C) They provide residents with the resources needed.) They provide residents with the resources needed. D) They allow free access to digital books and videos.) They allow free access to digital books and videos.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) By helping them find jobs.17.A)By helping them find jobs. B) By inspiring their creativity.)By inspiring their creativity. C) By keeping them off the streets.) By keeping them off the streets. D) By providing a place of relaxation.)By providing a place of relaxation.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Their interaction with teenagers proved fruitful.18.A)Their interaction with teenagers proved fruitful. B) They used libraries less often than teenagers.B)They used libraries less often than teenagers. C) They tended to visit libraries regularly.)They tended to visit libraries regularly. D) Their number increased modestly.) Their number increased modestly.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It is the cleverest cat in the world.19.A)It is the cleverest cat in the world. B) It is the largest cat in Africa.) It is the largest cat in Africa. C) It is an unusual cross breed.) It is an unusual cross breed. D) It is a large-sized wild cat.) It is a large-sized wild cat.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) They are as loyal as dogs.20.A) They are as loyal as dogs. B) They have unusually long tails.) They have unusually long tails. C) They are fond of sleeping in cabinets.) They are fond of sleeping in cabinets. D) They know how to please their owners.)They know how to please their owners.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) They shake their front paws.21.A)They shake their front paws. B) They teach them to dive.) They teach them to dive. C) They shower with them.) They shower with them. D) They shout at them.D) They shout at them.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Anxious and depressed.22.A) Anxious and depressed. B) Contented and relieved.) Contented and relieved. C) Excited but somewhat sad.) Excited but somewhat sad. D) Proud but a bit nervous.D) Proud but a bit nervous.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It is becoming parents’ biggest concern.23.A)It is becoming parents'biggest concern. B) It is gaining increasing public attention.)It is gaining increasing public attention. C) It is depends on their parents for success.)It is depends on their parents for success. D) It starts the moment they are born.D)It starts the moment they are born.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Set a good example for them to follow.4.A) Set a good example for them to follow. B) Read books and magazines to them.)Read books and magazines to them. C) Help them to learn by themselves.)Help them to learn by themselves. D) Choose the right school for them.D)Choose the right school for them.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Their intelligence.25.A) Their intelligence. B) Their home life.) Their home life. C) The effort they put in learning.)The effort they put in leaming. D) The quality of their school.)The quality of their school.","start":0,"end":0}],
