    "sentences": [{"text":"A) See the Pope. C) Travel to Germany. B) Go to Newcastle. D) Tour an Italian city.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) He was taken to hospital in an ambulance. B) His car hit a sign and was badly damaged. -8)-His-GPS-system-went out of-order;- D) He ended up in the wrong place.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Scotland will reach the national target in carbon emissions reduction ahead of schedule. B) Glasgow City Council has made a deal with ScottishPower on carbon emissions. C) Glasgow has pledged to take the lead in reducing carbon emissions in the UK. D) First Minister Nicola Sturgeon urged ScottishPower to reduce carbon emissions.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Glasgow needs to invest in new technologies to reach its goal. B) Glasgow is going to explore new sources of renewable energy. C) Stricter regulation is needed in transforming Glasgow's economy. D) It's necessary to create more low-emission zones as soon as possible.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It donates money to overpopulated animal shelters. B) It permits employees to bring cats into their office. C) It gives 5,000 yen to employees who keep pet cats. D) It allows workers to do whatever their hearts desire.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Keep cats off the street. C) Volunteer to help in animal shelters. B) Rescue homeless cats. D) Contribute to a fund for cat protection.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It has contributed tremendously to the firm's fame. B) It has helped a lot to improve animals' well-being. C) It has led some other companies to follow suit. D) It has resulted in damage to office equipment.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Find out where Jimmy is. C) Make friends with Jimmy. B) Borrow money from Jimmy. D) Ask Jimmy what is to be done.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) He was unsure what kind of fellow Jimmy was. B) He was working on a study project with Jimmy. C) He wanted to make a sincere apology to Jimmy. D) He wanted to invite her to join in a study project.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) He got a ticket for speeding. C) He was involved in a traffic accident. B) He got his car badly damaged. D) He had an operation for his injury.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) He needed to make some donation to charity. B) He found the 60 pounds in his pocket missing. C) He wanted to buy a gift for his mother's birthday. D) He wanted to conceal something from his parents.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Shopping delivery. C) Where he goes shopping. B) Shopping online. D) How often he does shopping.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Searching in the aisles. C) Driving too long a distance. B) Dealing with the traffic. D) Getting one's car parked.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) The after-sales service. C) The quality of food products. B) The replacement policy. D) The damage to the packaging.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It saves money. C) It increases the joy of shopping. B) It offers more choice. D) It is less time-consuming.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) They have little talent for learning math. B) They need\\_�«!dical help f�� math anxiety. C) They need extra help to catch up in the math class. D) They have strong negative emotions towards math.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It will gradually pass away without teachers' help. B) It affects low performing children only. C) It is related to a child's low intelligence. D) It exists mostly among children from poor families.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Most of them have average to strong math ability. B) Most of them get timely help from their teachers. C) They will regain confidence with counselling. D) They are mostly secondary school students.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Social media addiction is a threat to our health. B) Too many people are addicted to smartphones. C) Addiction to computer games is a disease. D) Computer games can be rather addictive.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) They prioritize their favored activity over what they should do. B) They do their favored activity whenever and wherever possible. C) They are unaware of the damage their behavior is doing to them. D) They are unable to get rid of their addiction without professional help.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It may be less damaging than previously believed. B) There will never be agreement on its harm to people. C) It may prove to be beneficial to developing creativity. D) There is not enough evidence to classify it as a disease.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) They are relatively uniform in color and design. B) They appear more formal than other passports. C) They are a shade of red bordering on brown. D) They vary in color from country to country.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) They must endure wear and tear. B) They must be of the same size. 24� -A7 -'Fhey- look-more-traditional-;- B) They look more official.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) For beauty. B) For variety. C) They must be made from a rare material. D) They must follow some common standards. C-) They are favored -by- airlines-; D) They are easily identifiable. C) For visibility. D) For security.","start":0,"end":0}],
