    "sentences": [{"text":"A) It studied the effects of exercise on sleep. B) Its participants came from various walks of life. C) Its findings confirmed those of previous studies. D) It ran for as long as some thirty years.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Eating more vegetables instead of meats. B) Drinking water instead of beverages with added sugar. C) Consuming more energy drinks and sports drinks. D) Forming the habit of exercising regularly.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) He asked them about his lost paintings. B) He knew the owner of two missing paintings. C) He left his paintings at a highway rest stop. D) He found two 17th-century oil paintings.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) They are imitations. C) They were stolen by an Italian boy. B) They are originals. D) They came from the same artist.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Look after her grandfather. C) Save her sick grandmother. B) Leave the remote cold region. D) Flee from the threat of bears.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) She has to face a criminal charge. B) She was found lying motionless in the snow. C) She searched for her daughter in freezing cold. D) She works in childcare services.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) She was found in a forest after three days. B) She lay totally unconscious for three days. C) She suffered from the effects of severe cold. D) She was finally rescued by her relatives.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) She shows a real passion for taking photos. B) She has just returned from her hometown. C) She comes from the city of Cape Town. D) She has a truly amazing appearance.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It is as famous as Cape Town. B) It has a flat surface at the top. C) It is green and free from pollution. D) It was named by European settlers.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) She has British ancestors. B) She is of mixed blood. C) She grew up in India. D) She speaks several languages.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It is an extremely violent sport. B) It is becoming a national sport. C) It is originated in New Zealand. D) It is more popular than football.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Prepare a study guide. B) Consult his advisors. C) Go over his notes regularly. D) Take stress-relief sessions.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) His worksheets are terribly messy. B) He finds the workload too heavy. C) His study folder is badly disorganized. D) He has difficulty taking notes quickly.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) A visual learner. B) An emotional learner. C) An organized learner. D) A logical learner.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Arrange them using color and pictures. B) Restructure them in a logical way. C) Commit them to memory after class. D) Organize them into a well-connected story.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It is mainly based on a society's religion. B) It is interpreted differently in different times. C) It is a code of conduct based on laws and ethics. D) It is a moral principle to guide people's behavior.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It may lead to misunderstanding despite good intentions. B) It assumes that human beings are all good-natured. C) It may sometimes produce undesirable outcomes. D) It fails to consider the complexity of human relationships.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) The golden rule is often in conflict with certain laws and ethical principles. B) The golden rule must sometimes give way to more important principles. C) Failure to follow the golden rule may lead to violation of laws and ethics. D) Observing the golden rule is the first step to becoming a responsible citizen.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Many of them find it rather difficult to manage. B) They have not seen as much diversity as desired. C) Many of them have an increasingly diversified staff. D) They have not quite grasped the concept of diversity.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Initiatives to achieve diversity in large corporations. B) Advantages and disadvantages of a diversified team. C) People's attitudes towards diversity at the workplace. D) Innovative ideas and solutions resulting from diversity.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) People prefer to work with team members similar to themselves. B) Employers attach great importance to their corporations' diversity. C) Employers differ, from employees in their perspectives on diversity. D) Doubts about the practicability of diversity are gradually disappearing.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Choosing the best time for signing a business contract. B) Changing one's form of communication from time to time. C) Laying equal stress on written and spoken communication. D) Using different forms of communication appropriately.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) They are regarded as seriously binding. B) They are seldom honored by business partners. C) They are taken as memos of understanding. D) They are to be confirmed in written form.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) It has reached the highest level of evolution. B) It places a high value on written contracts. C) It regards written contracts as unalterable. D) It has seen a decline in verbal agreements.","start":0,"end":0},{"text":"A) Its details cannot be renegotiated. B) It has to be carried out to the letter. C) It strengthens business partnerships. D) Its terms may not be strictly binding.","start":0,"end":0}],
